---
// The Blender ring: two self-chosen weeks of learning 3D modelling and printing.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Project from '../../layouts/Project.astro';
import render from '../../assets/ring-render.png';
import sketch from '../../assets/ring-moodboard.jpg';
import burger from '../../assets/burger-keychain.jpg';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
---

<Project
  title="My own ring"
  gallery
  summary="In my first internship I got two weeks to learn whatever I wanted. I picked Blender and 3D printing, and ended up with a ring I designed and printed myself."
  meta="Self-taught · two weeks in 2024 · Blender, Prusa Slicer, 3D printing"
  description="Two weeks of learning Blender and 3D printing during my internship, ending in a signet ring I designed and printed myself."
>
  <Image slot="media" loading="eager" src={render} alt="Render of a black signet ring with bone-like details, modelled in Blender" widths={[640, 960, 1400]} sizes="(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 960px" />

  <h2>The plan</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Follow a beginner tutorial to learn the basics.</li>
    <li>Model a burger for Chef Line’s Journey.</li>
    <li>Design a ring of my own.</li>
    <li>3D print what I made.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it went</h2>
  <p>
    Two days of tutorial, then the burger. I made it twice to try different ways of doing the cheese, one of them a
    cloth simulation, and used geometry nodes to place the sesame seeds. It became a keychain: my first 3D print.
  </p>
  <p>
    The second week went to the ring. The hardest part was a design I actually liked. After a lot of sketching I
    landed on a signet ring with bone-like shapes, and printed it on the office printer.
  </p>

  <h2>What I took from it</h2>
  <p>
    It’s how I still learn something new: get the basics from a tutorial, then go straight to something I actually
    want to make.
  </p>

  <figure slot="aside">
    <video src={`${base}media/ring-showcase.mp4`} autoplay muted loop playsinline aria-label="The printed ring held between fingers and worn on a hand"></video>
    <figcaption>The printed ring, on my hand.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <figure slot="aside">
    <Image src={sketch} alt="A sheet of hand-drawn cross and star shapes with bone-like ends, surrounded by handwritten notes" widths={[480, 760]} sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 380px" />
    <figcaption>Sketches and notes while looking for the ring’s shape.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <figure slot="aside">
    <Image src={burger} alt="A yellow 3D-printed burger keychain held between two fingers" widths={[480]} sizes="(max-width: 800px) 100vw, 380px" />
    <figcaption>My first print: the burger, in yellow PLA.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</Project>
